🚀 PROBLEM: TASK SCHEDULER
🔹 Problem Statement

You are given an array of characters tasks, where each character represents a task type.
You are also given an integer n representing the cooldown interval.

Each task takes 1 unit of time, and the same task must be separated by at least n units of time.

👉 Return the minimum number of time units required to complete all tasks.

Example
Input:  tasks = ['A','A','A','B','B','B'], n = 2
Output: 8

🔹 Why this problem is GOLD 🥇

✔ Very frequent in Google, Amazon, Microsoft
✔ Tests Greedy + Math + Heap intuition
✔ Multiple approaches (heap / formula)
✔ Shows problem-solving maturity

🔹 Key Insight 💡

The task with maximum frequency determines the idle slots.

🔹 Optimal Formula Approach (Most Expected in Interviews)

Let:

maxFreq = highest frequency of any task

countMax = number of tasks with frequency = maxFreq

Formula:
Answer = max(
    totalTasks,
    (maxFreq - 1) * (n + 1) + countMax
)

🔹 Dry Run Example 🧠
Input:
tasks = [A, A, A, B, B, B]
n = 2

Step 1 – Frequencies
A → 3
B → 3

Step 2 – Values
maxFreq = 3
countMax = 2

Step 3 – Formula
(3 - 1) * (2 + 1) + 2 = 2 * 3 + 2 = 8


✅ Answer = 8

🔹 Visual Intuition 📊
A _ _ A _ _ A
B _ _ B _ _ B


Fill gaps optimally → total = 8 units

🔹 Java Code (Formula-Based – BEST)
class Solution {
    public int leastInterval(char[] tasks, int n) {

        int[] freq = new int[26];

        // Count frequency
        for (char task : tasks) {
            freq[task - 'A']++;
        }

        int maxFreq = 0;
        for (int f : freq) {
            maxFreq = Math.max(maxFreq, f);
        }

        int countMax = 0;
        for (int f : freq) {
            if (f == maxFreq)
                countMax++;
        }

        int partCount = maxFreq - 1;
        int partLength = n + 1;
        int totalSlots = partCount * partLength + countMax;

        return Math.max(totalSlots, tasks.length);
    }
}

🔹 Line-by-Line Logic 🧩
partCount = maxFreq - 1;


➡ Number of gaps created by most frequent task

partLength = n + 1;


➡ Each gap needs space for cooldown

totalSlots = partCount * partLength + countMax;


➡ Total length after placing max tasks

Math.max(totalSlots, tasks.length)


➡ If no idle time needed → tasks length wins

🔹 Complexity
Metric	Value
Time	O(N)
Space	O(1)
